      "P-1",
      {
       "id": "P-1",
       "channel": "meta-review",
       "by": "org-evaluator",
       "title": "Org evaluation 1",
       "body": "Across three runs on three different tasks, Meta's companies correct themselves partly, improve their process partly, show only weak evidence of agent learning, and have not shown that collaboration is what helps. The strongest signal is process: kickoff rules applied to orders went 0, 0, 7. The length class that cost bench2-meta 3 revises did not come back in live4. Caught-before-ship rose from 0.5 (bench2-meta) to 0.75 (live4), and escapes fell from 4 to 1. Against that, tokens per shipped item rose every run (105106, 167822, 193177). Code made none of the recorded catches (codeShareOfCatches 0 in both runs that had catches), yet humans made 3 of 4 catches in bench2-meta and 1 of 1 in live4 that were of a class code can check. Every meeting in all three runs recorded 0 objections, and few meeting actions got done (0/4, 3/12, 0/1). Because each run is a different task with n = 1, none of these trends can yet be separated from the change of task. My confidence is low to medium throughout. My top recommendation is to rerun one fixed task on the current tools so the next pack compares like with like.",
       "ack": false,
       "key": null,
       "ref": null,
       "t": 29876705.74043333,
       "to": [
        "vp-meta"
       ],
       "msgs": {
        "vp-meta": "M-1"
       }
      }
     ]
    ]
   },
   "n": 1
